      "ReworkRequest and Rejection records; reviewSubmission reason validation; the Reject choice is hidden behind OFFER_REJECTION = false in ReviewPanel.tsx (hidden 2026-08-16, logic untouched — reviewSubmission still accepts \"rejected\" and the decision === \"rejected\" branch still renders), pinned by lib/rules/tasks/rejectionHidden.test.ts; TaskDetail.tsx's Reject decides an APPROVAL and is a different control; the rework deadline rule is lib/rules/tasks/reworkDeadline.ts (window = currentDeadline − submittedAt (the leftover), floored to whole seconds; on-time gate on the SUBMISSION is what keeps it non-negative), applied by reworkTask in grav-cms-backend/services/taskForward.service.js through computeWorkingDeadline so the hour walks the office calendar, and mirrored in the mock's reviewSubmission rework branch; the held reason travels as reworkHistory[].deadlineHeldReason and ReworkPanel.tsx renders it. The reviewer’s priority for the rework is ReworkQueuePicker.tsx over lib/rules/tasks/reworkQueue.ts — hidden behind OFFER_PRIORITY_CHOICE = false since 2026-08-18, logic untouched, pinned by lib/rules/tasks/reworkQueue.test.ts — sent as ReviewInput.reworkPriority and applied by reworkTask, which then calls rechainQueueFor for every assignee (added 2026-08-18). Replaced the leftover-time rule (deadline − submittedAt, added to a snapped now) 2026-08-16; the window was briefly rewritten to a flat hour and then to the task budget that day, before the owner's own figures (T044: 12:21 deadline, 12:17 submitted, 12:19 rework → 12:23) confirmed the leftover; their original example could not tell the rules apart because its leftover happened to equal one hour. The gate and the office-calendar walk are kept from those rewrites and were not in the original",
