    answer:
      "Tick **Mark as important** when you create a task, and it carries an **Important** tag — shown beside its status on the task itself and on every list it appears in, so it can be picked out without opening it. **It is a label and nothing else.** It does not change the order of your queue, the priority rank, the deadline, the score, or who may do what — a task tagged Important sits exactly where its priority puts it and is treated exactly as it would be without the tag. That is deliberate: it is a way of saying \"look at this one\" to the people reading the list, not a second priority system competing with the first. Two things it is often confused with. **Priority** — P1, P2, P3 — is the real ordering, and it decides which task your working hours are spent on first; the Important tag does not touch it. **Emergency mode** is a separate thing again, with its own approval and its own effect on deadlines. A task with no tag is the ordinary case, not a task that somebody forgot to mark. The tick is on the create form only: an existing task cannot be marked or unmarked from the screen yet.",
